   "d12: That night, they bring Tanya home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours.",
   "d14: You say a few words for Tanya. Not a ceremony — just: you were here, and someone noticed you leaving. (-3 trauma)",
   "d14: You bury Tanya. A marker, of sorts. The village will know where. (+4 trauma)",
   "d14: Not guilty. The count falls short — you breathe. But an accusation leaves a mark no verdict washes off. Some faces at the fire say they'll remember anyway.",
   "d14: ◈ The System files the name away with visible satisfaction. It has so few words for things that bleed. (+6 integration)"
